# Always commit and push after every step

After each completed step or user request that changes files in this project, commit and push to GitHub automatically — without waiting to be asked.

- Commit immediately when a discrete step of work is done (not only at the end of a long session)
- Push after each successful commit so GitHub Pages stays current
- Commit only when there are actual changes
- Do not push secrets or credential files
- Use the existing commit message style (concise, why-focused)
- Confirm the commit and push succeeded before finishing your response
